  "raw_text": "EncryptPad's format was adopted as the default encryption standard for the passphrase-based tool because interoperability with Windows machines requires the EncryptPad format for shared files. This cross-platform sharing constraint, rather than abstract preference, drove the choice of EncryptPad as the baseline while the SSH-key-based `seal_it` path serves the purely local sealing and backup workflow.",
